  "title": "Siege of Isfahan (1722)",
  "summary": "Afghan forces under Mahmud besieged the Safavid capital Isfahan from March to October 1722. Lacking artillery, they blockaded the city; starvation and disease followed, and one source estimates eighty thousand inhabitants died. On 23 October Sultan Husayn abdicated and acknowledged Mahmud as shah of Persia, after which the city was sacked.",
